docs {
  # POST /api/sales/ — Create sale with valid vip_code (tracking-only)

  Demonstrates `vip_code` `trim + case-insensitive + active=True` validation. Requires `Authorization: Token {{token}}`. Source: `travels/serializers.py:66-89` (`vip_code` `CharField(10) writeOnly`, `validate_vip_code:70` `value__iexact` + `active=True`, `validate:83` maps to `sale.vip_code`, `create:91` `transaction.atomic()`), `travels/views.py:94-126`, `travels/models.py:170` FK `PROTECT`.

  Body uses `"  vip123  "` (spaces + lowercase) to prove trimming and `iexact`. Any active `VipCode` value (e.g., `VIP123` in DB) matches.

  ## Status codes

  - `201 Created` — valid active vip_code, sale created with `Sale.vip_code` FK. Subsequent `GET /api/sales/?stripe_code={{stripe_code}}` returns `vip_code:"VIP123"` (stored value, upper as in DB).
  - `401 Unauthorized` — invalid/inactive vip_code (see `post_create_invalid_vip_code.bru`)
  - `400 Bad Request` — other validation errors

  ## Response (201)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Sale created successfully",
    "data": {
      "payment_link": "https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/..."
    }
  }
  ```

  `payment_link` prefix-only; `total` pricing-derived. `vip_code` is tracked, **no discount/bypass** — Stripe link always created (`views.py:101`).

  ## Notes

  - `PROTECT` blocks deletion of in-use codes (admin `ProtectedError`).
  - `transaction.atomic()` ensures no orphan `Client` on `401`.
}
